{"index":3163,"node_id":"74212776-cef4-4728-ad85-79a95deaf16d","parent":"21eb4797-3fd2-44bd-8fce-9345238d3393","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791154587.445705,"update_time":1791154587.445705,"content_type":"thoughts","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"thoughts\",\"thoughts\":[{\"summary\":\"Created and verified state machine specification trees, metadata, workflows, and manifests\",\"content\":\"\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true}],\"source_analysis_msg_id\":\"b57b2d7e-fcb5-454e-b523-335fdaaaace8\"}"}
{"index":3164,"node_id":"fd46c5ac-af73-4064-8fb2-7029770dc19a","parent":"74212776-cef4-4728-ad85-79a95deaf16d","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791154587.452476,"update_time":1791154587.452476,"content_type":"reasoning_recap","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"reasoning_recap\",\"content\":\"Worked for 10m 36s\"}"}
{"index":3165,"node_id":"d5db2a05-5a29-499e-ad22-e09e4a73bfb3","parent":"fd46c5ac-af73-4064-8fb2-7029770dc19a","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791154587.459512,"update_time":1791154604.644608,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Implemented.\n\nThe metadata is now **integral to each `.txt` document**. Each document begins with:\n\n```json\n{\"metadata\":{\"this\":\"metadata\",\"file_description\":\"...\"}}\n```\n\nThe `this` key is therefore exactly:\n\n```json\n\"this\": \"metadata\"\n```\n\nThis is verified in both the first and last section files. fileciteturn759file0L2-L5 fileciteturn760file0L2-L5 The existing report documents retain their body after the metadata line; for example, the main specification now starts with its metadata JSON and then the original specification text. fileciteturn762file0L2-L5\n\nI also changed `update-manifest.js` so it no longer reads a separate metadata registry. It reads the **first non-empty line of every `.txt` file**, parses that JSON, requires `metadata.this === \"metadata\"` and a non-empty `metadata.file_description`, and generates the manifest from it. fileciteturn761file0L2-L4\n\nThe standalone `metadata.json` was removed. The regenerated manifest now explicitly records its source as:\n\n```text\nembedded text-file JSON -> metadata.file_description\n```\n\nand also records the embedded metadata contract. fileciteturn765file0L2-L5\n\nThe automatic manifest workflow ran against the implementation commit and **completed successfully**. fileciteturn763file0L2-L2\n\nImplementation commit: `7babd1d529beaf321b84801cb5c9f4dac651e3e1`  \nCurrent `main` after the workflow regenerated the manifest: `db05ba8acd9294bad5e9d444d4e940046bd9f19e`"}
{"index":3166,"node_id":"bbb21a19-4c9f-4f83-9606-451f0273740e","parent":"d5db2a05-5a29-499e-ad22-e09e4a73bfb3","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791157435.230136,"update_time":1791157749.007379,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"We're going to create a yaml that lets you make configurable updates to the files in this folder. When triggered the script will use a list iterator to iterate a a list of lists, which will contain as an example a listA which contains arg1, arg2, etc for each arg in listA it executes A.js(arg). Then it will iterate thru listB which map a list of args to B.js "}
